<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siegfried of Westerburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1297">1297</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siegfried of Westerburg was archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> from 1275 until his death in 1297. He opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I of Brabant</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-limburg-succession">War of the Limburg Succession</a>, but was defeated and captured at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> in 1288. The defeat broke the archbishops' secular power in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>, and the city of Cologne, allied with Brabant, freed itself from their rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siegfried-of-westerburg.jpg" alt="Siegfried of Westerburg" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Janssen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Worringen_1288.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
